• changes in tax accounting rules or principles and in the valuation of deferred tax assets and liabilities;
• outcomes of income tax audits; and
• expiration or lapses of tax credits or incentives.
At the time we completed the Broadcom Merger, in connection with the preliminary allocation of purchase price, we established a deferred tax liability
on our balance sheet. This is associated with our potential tax liability arising from our planned integration of BRCM’s IP, which was completed in
November 2016. This tax liability will become payable as earnings resulting from this integration of IP is distributed over time. In addition, prior to the
closing of the Broadcom Merger, our policy was to indefinitely reinvest a portion of our foreign earnings to fund our operations outside Singapore. Effective
